course: dictionary
lesson: 1010
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Bond is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Pets bond with their families and miss them when they are alone.» Here bond means to become close to someone, because the sentence is about feelings and missing people.
explain: Now try a different context: «In ball-and-stick models, balls stand for atoms and sticks for bonds.» Here a bond is a link that holds atoms together, like a stick joining two balls. The word is the same, but the clues point to a different meaning. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Maths uses bond too. A number bond is a pair of numbers that make a total: 6 and 4 are a number bond to 10. When you see bond in a maths lesson, the clue is the numbers. When you see it with people or pets, the clue is feelings. Check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it makes sense.
fact: Bond can be a noun (a bond) or a verb (to bond).
fact: As a noun, a bond is a close feeling or connection between people or animals, such as friends or family.
fact: In science, a chemical bond holds atoms together in a molecule.
fact: In maths, «number bonds» are pairs of numbers that make a total, such as 3 and 7 make 10.
fact: A bond can also be the money paid when renting a home, called a deposit.
exercise: «Pets bond with their families and miss them when they are alone.» What does bond mean here? | To tie things together with string | To count in tens | *To become close to someone | To pay back money
exercise: In maths, what is a number bond? | A very large number | A sum that you cannot do | *Two numbers that make a total, like 6 and 4 | A ring of numbers on a clock
exercise: «In ball-and-stick models, balls stand for atoms and sticks for bonds.» What do the sticks stand for? | Carbon | *Links that hold atoms together | Atoms | Oxygen
test: «Pets bond with their families and miss them when they are alone.» Which sentence means the same as bond here? | *Pets become close to their families | Pets pay their families money | Pets count their families in tens | Pets tie their families together with string
test: Which pair is a number bond to 10? | *3 and 7 | 5 and 6 | 3 and 4 | 2 and 9
exam: Jayden reads «a bond holds atoms together» and «pets bond with their families». Why does bond mean different things in these sentences? | *The words around it show which meaning fits | The word is spelled differently each time | Bond always means the same thing in every sentence | One sentence is about science and the other is in a foreign language
